564 - For Sunrise Hope and Sunset Calm
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 564
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[C/E]For [Dm]sunrise [C]hope and [Dm]sunset [G]calm,
[C/E]And allthat [Dm]liesbetween,
[G7]For all [C]the sweetness [G]and the [C]balm
[C/E]That [Dm]isand [G]thathas [C]been,
[C/E]For [F]comradeship [C/E]for [G/D]peace in [Am]strife,
[Dm]And light [G]on darkened [Am]days;
[Dm]For work [G]to doand [Am]strength [Dm]for [G]life
[G7/D]We sing our [C]hymn of praise.

Verse 2:
[C/E]But O, [Dm]we [G]press far, far [C]above [Dm]these gifts of [G]pure delight,
[G7]And find [C]in Thee, and in [Dm]Thy love [G]contentment infinite.
[Dm]O Lord, beloved, [G]in whom are found all [Am]joys of time and place,
[G7/D]What will it be when joy is [C]crowned by vision of Thy face?
